  "pd": {
    "basis": "published-pre-1930",
    "detail": "First published 1902 by John Stark & Son, St. Louis; Joplin died in 1917, so the rag is free in the US and under life-plus-70 alike.",
    "sourceEdition": "Joplin, 'The Entertainer', John Stark & Son 1902 piano score, read via the Mutopia Project LilyPond engraving of that edition (typeset by Chris Sawer, overhauled by Simon Albrecht 2015, placed in the public domain by the typesetter) and cross-checked bar by bar against the CCARH Humdrum encoding of the same score",
    "notes": "Melody and harmony only; the rag is instrumental and carries no lyrics. Joplin wrote it in 2/4 with 16th-note figures. Encoded as 4/4 with each written bar becoming one encoded bar and every value doubled (written 16th becomes an encoded 8th), the standard cut-time mapping, so tempoBPM 152 is Joplin's quarter = 76. Ragtime is straight, never triplet. The famous D-D# pickup into the A strain lives at the end of the intro section. The C and D strains (the trio) are not carried in v1."
  },
